   "id": 631703,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "A water park charges $17 per entry plus a $40 fee for raft rentals. An amusement park charges a $21 entry fee.<br><br>For the number of entries, <span data-math=\"e\">e</span>, which inequality represents the total cost of the water park being less than the total cost of the amusement park?",
